    "title": "What we know about Shamonda, the livestock virus linked to a human infection for the first time | HT Explainers",
    "text": "The virus\nShamonda is an orthobunyavirus, the same type of virus as Schmallenberg, which spread through European livestock from 2011. Within that group, Shamonda is part of the Simbu serogroup, a family of more than 25 related viruses that the immune system recognises in similar ways. Several of its members, including Akabane and Schmallenberg, are carried by insects and can harm unborn livestock.",
